WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:04.480
I started out in that Institutional Foods Program.

2
00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:11.740
But my father said to me as I got on towards the junior and senior year, he said,

3
00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:18.960
“You know, you might think about what can you do to get a job with that now.

4
00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:24.640
And it might be smart to get your teacher’s certificate, just as security.”

5
00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.160
And so I thought that was a pretty good idea, too.

6
00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:37.760
I talked with the faculty at that time and I was able to elect in my junior and senior year all the courses that I would need to meet state certification requirements,

7
00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:43.640
because I had the other . . . I had all the science background,

8
00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:51.680
because I had the chemistry and so forth for the foods work that I was involved in.

9
00:00:51.680 --> 00:01:02.360
And I had general ed[ucation], sociology, and all those social sciences, so it was easy at that time to elect the education courses.

10
00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:04.020
So I elected student teaching.

11
00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:11.500
And I did my student teaching in Dutchtown, Louisiana, in Ascension Parish.

12
00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:18.180
At that time, that was an eleven-year school all in one building.

13
00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:24.800
And I loved the experience so much that I ended up . . . that’s all I ever did.
